        }
      },
      "input_state": "mixed pellets",
      "output_state": "as-cast ingot",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "2.1. Material preparation",
          "quote": "The mixed pellets were placed into a clean vacuum chamber of the arc-melting furnace with an in-place chill casting onto a water-cooled copper hearth. The chamber was sealed and then vacuumed to ~0.01 MPa. The chamber was then flushed with high-purity argon air and repetitively evacuated to eliminate the retained oxygen within the chamber. During arc-melting, two titanium getters were first melted to further absorb the remained oxygen to avoid the oxidation of pellets. Then, the mixed pellets were melted. In order to achieve a chemical composition homogeneity within the as-cast EHEAs ingots, melting was repeated for at least five times.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "0f247fad47f01709:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
